<!-- Question 1 -->

<div class="card" id="q1">

<h2>1. HTTP Response Analysis</h2>

<pre>
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Date: Mon, 01 Apr 2026 10:00:00 GMT
Content-Type: text/html
Content-Length: -150
Connection: keep-alive
</pre>

<h3>1. Invalid Fields</h3>

<div class="answer">
The Content-Length field is invalid because a negative value cannot represent the size of a response body.
</div>


<h3>2. Content-Length Issue</h3>

<div class="answer">
A negative Content-Length value can prevent browsers from interpreting the HTTP response correctly and may cause the webpage to fail loading.
</div>


<h3>3. Status Code Analysis</h3>

<div class="answer">
Although 200 OK indicates a successful response, the invalid header field makes the response technically incorrect.
</div>


<h3>4. Suggested Correction</h3>

<div class="answer">
Replace Content-Length: -150 with a valid positive value such as Content-Length: 150.
</div>

</div>



<!-- Question 2 -->

<div class="card" id="q2">

<h2>2. DOM Structure Analysis</h2>

<pre>
&lt;html&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
&lt;title&gt;Test Page&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hello World
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;
</pre>


<h3>1. Missing Elements</h3>

<div class="answer">
The paragraph tag (&lt;/p&gt;) is missing and the HTML structure is improperly closed.
</div>


<h3>2. Browser Interpretation</h3>

<div class="answer">
Modern browsers automatically insert missing tags whenever possible.
</div>


<h3>3. Rendering Impact</h3>

<div class="answer">
The page may still render correctly but is not standards compliant.
</div>


<h3>4. Suggested Correction</h3>

<div class="answer">
Close the paragraph element properly before the closing div tag.
</div>

</div>



<!-- Question 3 -->

<div class="card" id="q3">

<h2>3. GET vs POST in Login System</h2>

<table>

<tr>
<th>Method</th>
<th>URL Example</th>
<th>Visibility</th>
<th>Security</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>GET</td>
<td>/login?user=admin</td>
<td>Visible</td>
<td>Low</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>POST</td>
<td>/login</td>
<td>Hidden</td>
<td>Moderate</td>
</tr>

</table>


<h3>1. Data Transmission</h3>

<div class="answer">
GET transfers data through URLs whereas POST transfers data through the request body.
</div>


<h3>2. Suitable Method</h3>

<div class="answer">
POST is recommended for login systems because credentials are not exposed in the browser's address bar.
</div>


<h3>3. Security Risks</h3>

<div class="answer">
GET requests expose sensitive information in browser history and server logs.
</div>


<h3>4. Best Practices</h3>

<div class="answer">

<ul>

<li>Use POST requests.</li>
<li>Enable HTTPS.</li>
<li>Implement secure password hashing.</li>
<li>Use session management techniques.</li>

</ul>

</div>

</div>



<!-- Question 4 -->

<div class="card" id="q4">

<h2>4. HTML Code Inspection</h2>

<pre>
&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
&lt;title&gt;Sample&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Welcome
&lt;p&gt;This is a paragraph
&lt;img src="image.jpg"&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;
</pre>


<h3>1. Missing Tags</h3>

<div class="answer">
The closing tags for h1 and paragraph elements are missing.
</div>


<h3>2. Image Tag Issues</h3>

<div class="answer">
The image element should contain an alt attribute for accessibility.
</div>


<h3>3. Browser Handling</h3>

<div class="answer">
Browsers attempt to automatically correct minor HTML errors.
</div>


<h3>4. Correct Version</h3>

<pre>
&lt;h1&gt;Welcome&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a paragraph.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;img src="image.jpg"
alt="Sample Image"&gt;
</pre>

</div>



