<div class="card" id="q5">

<h2>5. Browser-Server Communication Flow</h2>

<ol>

<li>User enters a URL.</li>
<li>DNS Lookup.</li>
<li>HTTP Request.</li>
<li>Server Processing.</li>
<li>HTTP Response.</li>
<li>Browser Rendering.</li>

</ol>


<h3>1. Communication Process</h3>

<div class="answer">
The browser sends requests to the server and receives resources required for rendering webpages.
</div>


<h3>2. Possible Delays</h3>

<div class="answer">
Delays may occur during DNS lookup, network transmission, server processing, and browser rendering.
</div>


<h3>3. Role of DNS</h3>

<div class="answer">
DNS translates domain names into IP addresses and enables browsers to locate web servers.
</div>


<h3>4. Performance Optimization</h3>

<div class="answer">

<ul>

<li>DNS caching.</li>
<li>Browser caching.</li>
<li>Content Delivery Networks.</li>
<li>Resource compression.</li>
<li>Optimized server configurations.</li>

</ul>

</div>

